### UI Toolkit Operations
- Use `manage_ui_toolkit` for Unity UI Toolkit (UXML/USS) asset management.
  - `create_uxml` / `create_uss`: Create new UXML or USS files.
  - `get_uxml_content` / `get_uss_content`: Read existing UXML/USS file content.
  - `add_element`: Add a UI element to a UXML file (supports VisualElement, Label, Button, TextField, Toggle, Slider, ScrollView, ListView, DropdownField, etc.).
  - `remove_element`: Remove an element by name from UXML.
  - `set_attribute`: Set an attribute on a UXML element (text, value, label, tooltip, etc.).
  - `set_style`: Add or update inline style properties on a UXML element.
  - `add_class` / `remove_class`: Manage CSS class names on elements.
  - `add_binding`: Add a `binding-path` attribute for data binding.
  - `query_element` / `list_elements`: Find elements by name/class/type or list all elements.
  - `validate_uxml`: Validate UXML structure and report errors.
  - `create_panel_settings`: Create a PanelSettings asset for UI Document rendering.
  - `configure_ui_document`: Assign UXML and PanelSettings to a UIDocument component on a GameObject.
  - `list_ui_documents`: List all UIDocument components in the scene.
  - `create_editor_window_template`: Generate a C# EditorWindow class with UXML/USS wiring.
  - `create_custom_element_template`: Generate a C# custom VisualElement class.
  - `list_assets`: List all UXML or USS assets in the project.

